.TH "PERCH-BACKUP" "1" "" "perch" "perch manual"
.SH NAME
perch\-backup \- write a consistent SQLite backup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B perch backup [OPTIONS] <destination.db>
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Use SQLite's online backup API to write a consistent copy while serve is running. The destination must not already exist.
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Safe alongside serve because SQLite WAL mode allows concurrent readers and writers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config <value>
configuration file (default: ~/.config/perch/perch.yaml)
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
show help
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
perch backup \-\-config /etc/perch/perch.yaml /var/lib/perch/backups/perch\-$(date +%F).db
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBperch\fR(1)
